Specification WorkedExample

Description One month of downloads, read into four accounts, and then worked
Description the way a person works it.
Details Every other file here specifies one thing at a time. This one is an
Details ordinary month end to end: four statements arrive as CSV, they are
Details imported, the categories that matter are assigned, and the report is
Details read. It is the book the window is tried against, written down, so
Details that what was being checked by hand is checked by the suite.
Details
Details What makes it worth having is that nothing in it is isolated. The
Details import, the chart of accounts, the categorisation and the report all
Details have to agree, and a change to one of them that breaks another shows
Details up here rather than in a month's time.
Details
Details Every scenario below is written against the Background alone, which is
Details inlined into each generated test, so none of them depends on the one
Details before it. That is why the same figures appear more than once: each
Details scenario starts from the four statements and nothing else.
Details
Details Opening balances are not in it. These are four downloads covering one
Details month, which is what keeps the book small enough to read on a page; a
Details book that starts from a known position is the opening-balance
Details transaction in Accounts. It is also why the loan here is a month of
Details interest rather than a debt being paid down.
Details
Details The statements do not carry each other's transfers. A card statement
Details closes on the twentieth and the payment goes out on the twenty-fifth,
Details so the payment is in the checking file and not in the card file, and
Details nothing is imported twice. Two downloads that do both show the same
Details transfer is a real situation and a different problem -- the matching
Details in ImportOfx -- and it is deliberately not what this file is about.

Background A month of statements, one for each account
Description Four accounts, two profiles, four files. The categories the
Description scenarios use are in the chart from the start, so that a scenario
Description is about assigning one and not about creating it.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                    | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking         | Bank       | false       |
| Assets:Savings          | Bank       | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa        | CreditCard | false       |
| Liabilities:Car Loan    | Liability  | false       |
| Expenses:Auto           | Expense    | true        |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel      | Expense    | false       |
| Expenses:Groceries      | Expense    | false       |
| Expenses:Home           | Expense    | true        |
| Expenses:Home:Repairs   | Expense    | false       |
| Expenses:Medical        | Expense    | true        |
| Expenses:Medical:Dental | Expense    | false       |
| Expenses:Shopping       | Expense    | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized  | Expense    | false       |
| Income:Uncategorized    | Income     | false       |
Given the csv profile is : CsvProfile Vertical
| Name         | Bank Download |
| HasHeader    | true          |
| DateColumn   | Date          |
| DateOrder    | MDY           |
| PayeeColumn  | Payee         |
| CheckColumn  | Check         |
| AmountStyle  | Signed        |
| AmountColumn | Amount        |
| OutwardSign  | Negative      |
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
Given the file contains
"""
Date,Payee,Check,Amount
03/02/2026,Acme Payroll,,2500.00
03/06/2026,Harris Teeter,,-84.50
03/09/2026,Durham Plumbing,1021,-275.00
03/12/2026,Chapel Hill Dental,1022,-140.00
03/25/2026,Visa Payment,,-200.00
"""
Given rows imported
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Savings |
Given the file contains
"""
Date,Payee,Check,Amount
03/03/2026,Deposit,,1000.00
03/31/2026,Interest Paid,,1.25
"""
Given rows imported
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Liabilities:Car Loan |
Given the file contains
"""
Date,Payee,Check,Amount
03/10/2026,Interest Charged,,-18.75
"""
Given rows imported
Given the csv profile is : CsvProfile Vertical
| Name         | Card Download |
| HasHeader    | true          |
| DateColumn   | Posted        |
| DateOrder    | MDY           |
| PayeeColumn  | Description   |
| AmountStyle  | Signed        |
| AmountColumn | Amount        |
| OutwardSign  | Negative      |
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Liabilities:Visa |
Given the file contains
"""
Posted,Description,Amount
03/05/2026,SHELL OIL 3344,-52.10
03/11/2026,AMAZON MARKETPLACE,-129.99
03/18/2026,HARRIS TEETER #231,-63.40
"""
Given rows imported

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What arrived
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Scenario The four registers balance after the imports
Description The first thing to check, and the thing a person checks: each
Description register agrees with the statement it was read from. A card and a
Description loan read as what is owed.
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account              | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes                      |
| Assets:Checking      | 1800.50    | 1800.50        | 2500.00 in, 699.50 out     |
| Assets:Savings       | 1001.25    | 1001.25        | A deposit and its interest |
| Liabilities:Visa     | -245.49    | 245.49         | Three charges, owed        |
| Liabilities:Car Loan | -18.75     | 18.75          | A month of interest        |
# Nothing has been categorised yet, so the other side of every one of these is
# Uncategorized -- chosen by the sign, so money in is Income:Uncategorized and
# money out is Expenses:Uncategorized. That is the work the scenarios below do.

Scenario Everything starts in Uncategorized
Description Not one of these files carried a category, so the whole month is
Description sitting in the two Uncategorized accounts waiting to be told what
Description it was. This is the state a month starts in, and the reason the
Description report is worth running at all.
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2026-03-01 |
| To       | 2026-03-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount  | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 3501.25 | true       |
| Income:Uncategorized   | 1     | 3501.25 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | 963.74  | true       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | 963.74  | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 3501.25 |
| TotalExpenses | 963.74  |
| Net           | 2537.51 |
# 2500.00 of salary, 1000.00 deposited and 1.25 of interest on one side; on the
# other, 84.50, 275.00, 140.00 and 200.00 from the checking account, 18.75 of
# loan interest, and 52.10, 129.99 and 63.40 on the card. The net is right and
# says nothing at all about where the money went, which is the whole point of
# categorising.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working the month
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Attributes CategoryAssignment
Description One transaction given its category. It is named by its date and
Description its payee, which is how a person finds it on the screen, rather
Description than by a ref: a ref is a device of these tables and is not
Description something the program shows.
| Attribute | Type        | Default |
| Date      | Date        |         |
| Payee     | PayeeName   |         |
| Category  | AccountPath |         |

Scenario Categorising the card charges and the two checks
Description The three charges on the card and the two checks written during
Description the month. The rest is left alone on purpose: the groceries bought
Description on the checking account and the payment to the card are still
Description Uncategorized afterwards, and the report shows them that way.
When categories assigned : CategoryAssignment
| Date       | Payee              | Category                |
| 2026-03-05 | SHELL OIL 3344     | Expenses:Auto:Fuel      |
| 2026-03-11 | AMAZON MARKETPLACE | Expenses:Shopping       |
| 2026-03-18 | HARRIS TEETER #231 | Expenses:Groceries      |
| 2026-03-09 | Durham Plumbing    | Expenses:Home:Repairs   |
| 2026-03-12 | Chapel Hill Dental | Expenses:Medical:Dental |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2026-03-01 |
| To       | 2026-03-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                 | Level | Amount  | IsSubtotal |
| Income                  | 0     | 3501.25 | true       |
| Income:Uncategorized    | 1     | 3501.25 | false      |
| Expenses                | 0     | 963.74  | true       |
| Expenses:Auto           | 1     | 52.10   | true       |
| Expenses:Auto:Fuel      | 2     | 52.10   | false      |
| Expenses:Groceries      | 1     | 63.40   | false      |
| Expenses:Home           | 1     | 275.00  | true       |
| Expenses:Home:Repairs   | 2     | 275.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Medical        | 1     | 140.00  | true       |
| Expenses:Medical:Dental | 2     | 140.00  | false      |
| Expenses:Shopping       | 1     | 129.99  | false      |
| Expenses:Uncategorized  | 1     | 303.25  | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 3501.25 |
| TotalExpenses | 963.74  |
| Net           | 2537.51 |
# The expenses total has not moved and neither has the net: categorising says
# where money went, not how much of it there was. A report whose total changed
# when a category was assigned would mean a posting had been lost, and that is
# worth checking on every one of these.
#
# What is left in Expenses:Uncategorized is 84.50 of groceries bought on the
# checking account, the 200.00 paid to the card and 18.75 of loan interest. The
# payment belongs in no category at all -- it is a transfer -- which is the
# next scenario. Income:Uncategorized still holds all three deposits: the
# salary is income and so is the interest, and the 1000.00 deposit is whatever
# it was, which this book does not say.

Scenario A payment to a card is a transfer, not an expense
Description Giving the payment the card account as its category makes the
Description transaction a transfer between two real accounts, and a transfer
Description is in no report of what was earned or spent. This is the one kind
Description of recategorisation that is allowed to move the total, because
Description both postings have left the categories altogether.
When categories assigned : CategoryAssignment
| Date       | Payee        | Category         |
| 2026-03-25 | Visa Payment | Liabilities:Visa |
When report run : ReportSpec Vertical
| GroupBy  | Category   |
| From     | 2026-03-01 |
| To       | 2026-03-31 |
| Interval | Whole      |
Then report rows are : ReportRow
| Account                | Level | Amount  | IsSubtotal |
| Income                 | 0     | 3501.25 | true       |
| Income:Uncategorized   | 1     | 3501.25 | false      |
| Expenses               | 0     | 763.74  | true       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | 1     | 763.74  | false      |
Then report total is : ReportTotal Vertical
| TotalIncome   | 3501.25 |
| TotalExpenses | 763.74  |
| Net           | 2737.51 |
Then balances are : AccountBalance
| Account          | RawBalance | DisplayBalance | Notes                      |
| Assets:Checking  | 1800.50    | 1800.50        | A recategory moves nothing |
| Liabilities:Visa | -45.49     | 45.49          | 245.49 charged, 200.00 paid |
# 963.74 less the 200.00 that was never an expense. The checking balance is
# untouched: the payment left the account either way, and all that changed is
# what the other side of it was called.
#
# The card is the figure worth looking at. Three charges came to 245.49, the
# payment was 200.00, and 45.49 is owed -- which is what the statement would
# say, and is only believable because the register adds up to it.
